  data: {
    LLM: 'Game: Auction Bridge. Type: Partnership bidding. Rules: 52 cards. Ranks: NT=10, S=9, H=8, D=7, C=6. All tricks over 6 count for game if contract made. Goal: Win two games (30 pts each) for the Rubber.',
    Player: 'Welcome to Auction Bridge. You have 13 cards. Unlike modern Bridge, every trick you win above six will count toward the game if you make your contract. The target is 30 points. Will you start with 1 Heart or try for a No Trump?',
    objective: "Score 'Below the Line' points by winning tricks to reach 30 points for a 'Game'. Win two games to win the 'Rubber'.",
    gameplay: "1. **Lead**: Player to declarer's left leads. 2. **Dummy**: Declarer's partner lays cards face up. Declarer plays both hands. 3. **Trick Rules**: Must follow suit if possible. Highest trump or led suit wins. 4. **Scoring**: If contract is made, ALL tricks over 6 score towards the game (e.g., if you bid 1 and win 3, all 3 count toward the game).",
    keyRules: [
      'Trick Values: No Trump (10), Spades (9), Hearts (8), Diamonds (7), Clubs (6).',
      "Honors: High cards (A, K, Q, J, 10 of trumps) score separate bonus points 'Above the Line'.",
      'Rubber: The first team to win two games of 30 points each wins the Rubber bonus (250 points).',
    ],
